$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure of NHS-Ester Coupling. In a round-bottom flask the
FMOC-protected ester, 1.1 equiv Nhydroxysuccinimide, 1.1 equiv
N,N-diisopropyl carbodiimide, and 1.1 equiv triphenylamine were suspended
in CH2Cl2 and stirred for 1 h. After this time, 0.5 equiv of
4,4′-bis(methylamine)-2,2′-bipyridine were added and the reaction stirred
for an additional 2 h. Purification was accomplished by filtration and
washing with minimal CH2Cl2 (2 × 5 mL).
4,4′-Bis(methylamido-Tyr(tBu)-N-FMOC)-2,2′-bipyridyl, b. Yield (isolated)
2.5 g, 98%. 1H NMR (N,N-DMF-d 7, 400 MHz): δ 8.77 (m, 2H, ArH), 8.59 (m,
2H, ArH), 8.42 (s, 2H, ArH), 7.93 (d, 2H, ArH), 7.73 (m, 2H, ArH), 7.44
(m, 2H, ArH), 7.33 (m, 4H, ArH), 7.07 (m, 4H, ArH), 6.89 (d, 2H, ArH),
5.56 (br m, 4H, -CH2NHC(O)R), 4.55 (m, 6H, -CH2-), 4.19 (m, 6H, -CH2-),
3.22 (m, 2H, -CH(CH2-)-), 2.99 (m, 2H, -CH(CH2-)-), 1.23 (br s, 18H, -CH
3). Elemental Analysis for C68H68N6O8·0.5CH2Cl2 Calc’d: C 72.18, H 6.10,
N 7.37; Found: C 71.30, H 6.35, N 8.70. ESI-MS (m/z) [M + H]+: Calc’d
1097.52. Found: 1097.74.
